  "description": "meme-id: partial_arts; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two individuals in martial arts uniforms, one adult and one child, standing in a grassy area in front of a house. The text \"partial arts\" is superimposed, creating a pun that implies the martial arts are only partially practiced or incomplete. The overall intent is to humorously suggest that the martial arts are not fully developed or are being performed in a half-hearted or inadequate manner. This meme is not inherently abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic. However, it can be considered harmful because it trivializes the discipline and seriousness of martial arts by reducing it to a joke about incompleteness, which may disrespect practitioners or the art form itself. The humor is derived from the juxtaposition of the serious martial arts attire and stance with the ironic, dismissive text, implying a lack of commitment or skill.",
